g UV coordinates, textures, color manipulation, the graphics pipeline, and GPU parallel processing. Demonstrates practical examples like creating circles, gradients, noise effects, and texture transformations through step-by-step exercises.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/J9qx8MxuJYM/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-02-15T11:00:34.000Z"},{"id":"gsdwJlz5x","title":"Build Stardew Valley clone with advanced Godot features","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jIKuiUdCsuo","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/recreate-stardew-valley-in-godot-and-master-advanced-godot-concepts-gsdwjlz5x","summary":"Comprehensive tutorial covering advanced Godot features by recreating Stardew Valley mechanics. Demonstrates animation trees, state machines, blend spaces, enums, tile map layers with terrains, and resource management. Walks through implementing player movement, tool switching, farming systems, and level design using autotiling. Includes practical exercises for mastering complex animation logic and input handling patterns.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/jIKuiUdCsuo/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":39,"num_comments":1,"created_at":"2025-12-06T10:56:56.000Z"},{"id":"m8brTfWlj","title":"Learn to code by making games in Godot","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TLG2yVpLDT8","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/learn-to-code-by-making-games-in-godot-m8brtfwlj","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/TLG2yVpLDT8/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-10-16T12:35:18.000Z"},{"id":"KlZb2isgz","title":"Master UI layouts in Godot with Zelda-style menus","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ny4JDxwlrbo","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/master-godot-layouts-by-recreating-zelda-uis-klzb2isgz","summary":"Learn how to master UI layouts in Godot by recreating Zelda-style menus. The tutorial covers essential topics such as integrating layouts in 2D games, handling controller input, and working with themes and animations. By the end, you will be able to create custom user interfaces in various styles, enhancing your game development skills.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Ny4JDxwlrbo/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":14,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-03-09T12:00:28.000Z"},{"id":"c0ON97NTC","title":"The ultimate introduction to Raylib","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UoAsDlUwjy0","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/the-ultimate-introduction-to-raylib-c0on97ntc","summary":"Learn how to use Raylib to create both 2D and 3D games. Raylib is popular for enabling advanced game development without requiring game engines like Unity. This tutorial, using Python, covers the basics such as setting up a window, drawing shapes, working with images and textures, handling input, and managing movement. It also introduces concepts like frame rate independence and vector math for game development.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/UoAsDlUwjy0/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":18,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-12-22T11:59:51.000Z"},{"id":"A8ewxIn8M","title":"Step-by-Step Guide to Building a Zelda: Breath of the Wild Style Game in Godot","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AoGOIiBo4Eg","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/recreating-zelda-breath-of-the-wild-in-godot-the-ultimate-intro-to-3d-game-dev--a8ewxin8m","summary":"This comprehensive tutorial guides you through creating a Zelda: Breath of the Wild inspired game in Godot. It serves as an introduction to 3D game development, covering basics such as managing 3D graphics, animations, interactivity, and level creation. Advanced topics like lighting, special effects, and shaders are also discussed to enhance the game's visual appeal. Basic knowledge of Godot engine and GD script is suggested for better understanding.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/AoGOIiBo4Eg/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":50,"num_comments":2,"created_at":"2024-11-10T10:08:01.000Z"},{"id":"TxqfK5rFg","titl